# Merge behaviour for shared append-only registries.
#
# Copy to the repository root as `.gitattributes`. Everything here is built
# into git — no `git config` in any clone, no hook installation, nothing that
# can be silently missing on someone else's machine. That property is the whole
# reason these entries are here rather than in a setup script.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What `merge=union` does, and the two ways it bites
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Union merge keeps BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of raising a
# conflict. For append-only lists that is usually what you want. Two hazards
# come with it, and both are silent:
#
#   1. EDIT vs EDIT. Two branches rewording the same line yield both wordings,
#      one after the other, with no conflict raised and nobody prompted.
#
#   2. APPEND vs PROMOTE. One branch appends to a section while another moves
#      that whole section somewhere else (a release promoting [Unreleased] into
#      a version heading). The appended line merges into a section that is no
#      longer where it was, and no test fails when it lands in the wrong place.
#
# So union merge on its own converts a loud conflict into a quiet corruption.
# It is only safe when a gate downstream can still see the damage. Here that
# gate is the drift check: the generated files below are assembled from their
# fragment directories, so any union artefact makes the committed file differ
# from what the generator produces, and CI rejects it with the fix in the
# failure message. Union + drift check is self-healing; union alone is a
# downgrade on doing nothing.
#
# If you remove the drift check from CI, remove these entries too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts — assembled from the fragment directory beside each one.
# Never hand-edited, so a union merge here cannot lose authored content: the
# fragments are the source, and regenerating restores the file exactly.
# `linguist-generated` collapses them in review so nobody reviews the assembly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHANGELOG.md                        merge=union linguist-generated=true
docs/DEBUGGING-KNOWLEDGE-BASE.md    merge=union linguist-generated=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fragments — one file per entry. These need no merge driver at all: two
# branches adding entries add different paths, and git merges disjoint file
# additions without being asked. The entries below are here to say so out
# loud, because an absent line looks like an oversight rather than a decision.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
changelog.d/**                      -merge
docs/DEBUGGING-KNOWLEDGE-BASE.d/**  -merge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registries you have not migrated yet
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Translation bundles, message-code catalogues and entity registries are the
# same shape and fail the same way. Until they are fragment-backed, union merge
# is the stopgap — but only alongside a uniqueness gate over their keys, for
# the reason above. Uncomment and adapt:
#
# src/i18n/*.json                   merge=union
# src/messages/message-codes.json   merge=union

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A warning about the obvious next step
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A CUSTOM merge driver (`merge=mydriver`) does NOT work from this file alone:
# it needs `git config merge.mydriver.driver ...` in every clone, and when that
# is missing git falls back silently — the file appears configured and is not.
# `union` is built in and has no such requirement. If you ever ship a custom
# driver, ship the bootstrap that configures it AND a check that verifies the
# config actually took effect in the clone that is running.
